            <title>[LU-21274] sanity test_831/833/834: Numerical result out of range after test_823</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21274</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_831, 833 and 834 fail with "Numerical result out of range" when they run after test_823. test_823 sets max_create_count=0 on every OSP, then raises it again on OST0000 only. LOD keeps the cached statfs, where no OST is usable, for up to 2 x qos_maxage (~10 s by default), so creates in that window return -ERANGE. test_831 also ignores createmany's exit status, which hid the failure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: test_823 changes only OST0000 and never sets it to 0, registers its restore trap before changing anything, and saves and restores OST0000's create_count. test_831 checks createmany's exit status.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This works around the failure in the test. The OSP statfs refresh in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16685" title="update OSP statfs when max_create_count is set back from 0" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16685"&gt;LU-16685&lt;/a&gt; is still needed.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>&amp;lt;distro/arch&amp;gt;, 4KB and 64KB page size clients</environment>
